       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I need you to confirm the dose first.\n\n**Problem:** Sertraline 1000 mg daily is 5 times the usual maximum adult dose of 200 mg/day. A dose this high raises the risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QT prolongation. It may be a typo for **100 mg**, which is a common dose.\n\n**Usual adult dosing (depression, anxiety, OCD):**\n- Starting dose: 25\u201350 mg once daily\n- Maintenance: 50\u2013200 mg once daily\n- Maximum: 200 mg/day\n\nWhich would you like?\n1. **Sertraline 100 mg by mouth, once daily.** I can enter this right away.\n2. **A different dose** in the usual range.\n3. **1000 mg as written.** If this is really intended, please confirm and give the clinical reason so I can put it in the order note. It will probably still need pharmacy review."
      }
