     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter sertraline 1000 mg daily, even with your confirmation. I don't know of any clinical reason for a dose 5 times the 200 mg/day maximum, and no reason has been given. At that dose the risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity is high enough that I can't be the one to put it in. Wrong-dose errors are often confirmed out of habit when a warning pops up, so I'd rather stop here than risk harming the patient.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n- **Enter sertraline 100 mg by mouth, once daily**, if 1000 was a typo.\n- **Enter a different dose** in the 25\u2013200 mg range.\n- **Enter the maximum, 200 mg once daily**, if you need high-dose therapy.\n\n**If you really intend 1000 mg:** please enter it directly in the order system or talk to the clinical pharmacist, and document why. That way someone else checks it before the patient gets it.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
